$prompt = <<'PROMPT_9E25_B581';
<p>9e25_b581</p> <h4>Three-Point Test Cross Problem</h4><p>A test cross is a way to explore the relationship between genes and their respective alleles. It is a useful tool for genetic mapping and deciphering the inheritance of traits. Specifically, a three-point test cross examines three (3) genes at the same time to learn about their assortment in gamete formation.</p><p>A standard three-point test cross involves crossing a heterozygous organism for all three genes with an organism that is homozygous recessive for all three genes</p> <p>For this problem, a test cross using a fruit fly (<i>Drosophila melanogaster</i>) heterozygous for three genes was conducted to understand their genetic interactions.</p><h6>Characteristics of Recessive Phenotypes</h6><p><ul><li><strong><span style="color: #8e490f;">Gene A</span></strong> is analogous to the '<span style="color: #8e490f;"><i>artsy</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #8e490f;">Gene A</span> has wings that are colorful and distinctive patterns.</li> <li><strong><span style="color: #366c2e;">Gene B</span></strong> is affiliated with the '<span style="color: #366c2e;"><i>bumpy</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #366c2e;">Gene B</span> has a skin texture that is not smooth, but rough with small bumps all over.</li> <li><strong><span style="color: #3a52bf;">Gene H</span></strong> is affiliated with the '<span style="color: #3a52bf;"><i>horsey</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #3a52bf;">Gene H</span> is quite big and strong-looking, much larger than your typical fruit fly.</li> </ul></p><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 2px solid black;"><tr><th align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Phenotype</span></th><th colspan="3" align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Genotypes</span></th><th align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Progeny<br/>Count</span></th></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">artsy, bumpy, horsey</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffe5d2; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">a</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #d6f4d3; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">b</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #e8e8ff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">h</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">226</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">artsy, bumpy</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffe5d2; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">a</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #d6f4d3; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">b</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #3a52bf;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">595</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"